@title STORY • NICOLE: CAPTAIN
@bg soccer_pitch_night
You're Nicole Miller. Captain. Forward. Denver. You've been captain since you were a sophomore, and you've been scared every day of it.
@show valentina
Valentina: You're doing the captain voice again.
Nicole: I don't have a captain voice.
Valentina: (deepening her voice) "Everybody, LINE UP." That's the captain voice.
> [Bitchy] "At least I don't have a talking-to-three-guys voice." -> a1
> [Sweet] Laugh. She's your best friend, even when she's not. -> a2
*a1
@add Valentina_Beef 2
Valentina: Okay. Wow. Okay.
And there it is. The fight again. You started it this time. You know you did.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Valentina_Bond 3
Valentina: (bumping your shoulder) See? You're fun when you let yourself be.
*a_done
@bg dorm_room_night
Your brother Noah calls. He always calls on bad nights. You've never told him which nights are bad. He just knows.
Noah: Talk.
> [Sweet] "I'm scared I'm a bad captain." -> b1
> [Good] "Valentina and I keep fighting over stupid guys." -> b2
*b1
@add Self 3
Noah: (quiet) Nic. You care so much it makes you crazy. That's not a bad captain. That's just a tired one.
@jump end
*b2
@add Valentina_Bond 2
Noah: Is it about the guys? Or is it that you're scared she'll find a best friend who isn't you?
You don't answer. He's right. He's always annoyingly right.
*end
Nicole Miller holds the whole team on her shoulders. This year, she's learning it's okay to put some of it down.
